<div class="rp-section">
  <div class="rp-section-head">
    <span class="rp-eyebrow">The Standard</span>
    <h2>Five Rules Every Appliance Follows</h2>
    <p>An image earns <code>type: appliance</code> only when it behaves like hardware: predictable name, zero day-one config files, and built-in observability.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ap-principles-grid">
    <div class="rp-mode-card">
      <span class="rp-mode-index">01 · Utilitarian Naming</span>
      <h3>Named for the job</h3>
      <p>Names state exactly what the box does — <code>reverse-proxy</code>, <code>pkg-cache</code> — never an opaque internal codename.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rp-mode-card">
      <span class="rp-mode-index">02 · Zero-Config Day One</span>
      <h3>Works on first boot</h3>
      <p>Starts cleanly from a single <code>fjord install</code> or <code>podman-compose up -d</code>. Environment variables tune behavior; they never gate startup.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rp-mode-card">
      <span class="rp-mode-index">03 · Self-Contained</span>
      <h3>No external sidecars</h3>
      <p>Bundles its own embedded state and supervisor so infrastructure never depends on a separate database container staying healthy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rp-mode-card">
      <span class="rp-mode-index">04 · Disposable Rootfs</span>
      <h3>One clean volume</h3>
      <p>Containers stay ephemeral and replaceable. Certificates, encrypted backups, or cached packages live on a single explicit mount.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rp-mode-card">
      <span class="rp-mode-index">05 · Instant Telemetry</span>
      <h3>Built-in UI &amp; healthz</h3>
      <p>Ships with a focused web interface, CLI helpers, and machine-readable health endpoints so you can verify operation in seconds.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="rp-section" markdown>
??? note "Contributor Reference: Marking an Image with `type: appliance`"

    To classify a repository as a Daemonless Appliance, set `type: appliance` under `x-daemonless` in `compose.yaml`:

    ```yaml
    x-daemonless:
      title: "Daemonless pkg cache"
      type: appliance
      category: "DevOps"
    ```

    `dbuild lint` validates `type` against `app`, `base`, `stack`, and `appliance` — see the [Configuration Reference](dbuild/config.md#metadata-x-daemonless) for full schema details.
</div>
